  "zoom": 1
}


:: Alleyway {"position":"800,350","size":"100,100"}
<img
class="fit-picture"
src="https://www.shutterstock.com/image-vector/magnifying-glass-icon-white-on-260nw-1059366797.jpg"
>
(set: $evidence to "tunnelSystem")
A dark alleyway is the perfect place to search for crime, being secluded and hidden away from most eyes.

Arriving at an alley in the neighborhood, initially nothing seems out of the ordinary, at least for a dark alley like this. Bottles, old newspapers, rotting corpses, garbage bags, just usual dirty alley stuff. However, looking behind a garbage container, you find a tunnel that leads to a large connection of tunnels. Exploring it you find a room with several floor boards used as its walls, with more floor boards used for furnishing. Using gloves to handle them, you take a few floorboards to check for fingerprints.

Testing the boards for prints, you find they all contain fingerprints matching to Flurob Burt.

[[Find culprit]]


:: Chase them down {"position":"1400,500","size":"100,100"}
<img
class="fit-picture"
src="https://www.shutterstock.com/image-vector/magnifying-glass-icon-white-on-260nw-1059366797.jpg"
>
(set: $captureMethod to "chase")
Before Flurob can even get far, you sprint after him so he won't get away. Running after him, you eventually tackle Flurob into the ground amd apprehend him before he gets too far. Once you do, you report to the police that you have him apprehended (if: $evidence is "policeSketch")[to their suprise. They did not expect that you would be that dedicated to the case, considering you hardly helped with the investigation. Regardless, they thank you for helping capture Flurob] and shortly after he is arrested.

[[Now that he has been caught, it is time to put the culprit to trial|Put the culprit to trial]]


:: Community Service {"position":"2000,200","size":"100,100"}
<img
class="fit-picture"
src="https://tse2.mm.bing.net/th/id/OIP.UyWnzzv2q5T4qkB8LzoxGgHaEK?rs=1&pid=ImgDetMain&o=7&rm=3"
>
(set: $sentence to "service")
(if: $evidence is "policeSketch" or $captureMethod is "policeReport")[While the jury is unsure why you feel you get a say in Flurob's punishment, as you let the police do most of the work, they agree with your decision. ]In the end, it was only floorboards and he had no intention of harming anyone. So with your reccomendation, the sentence of Flurob Burt was 5 years of community service to replace the stolen floors (if: $evidence is "tunnelSystem")[and filling in the tunnels he dug out].

[[Ending]]


:: Death sentence {"position":"2000,500","size":"100,100"}
<img
class="fit-picture"
src="https://tse2.mm.bing.net/th/id/OIP.UyWnzzv2q5T4qkB8LzoxGgHaEK?rs=1&pid=ImgDetMain&o=7&rm=3"
>
Flurob Burt has stolen an uncountable amount of value in floorboards, and was negligent to the several lives he endangered. For this, he faces the death sentence so he may never endanger anyone ever again. (set: $sentence to "death")

[[Ending]]


:: Ending {"position":"2175,350","size":"100,100"}
<img
class="fit-picture"
src="https://thumbs.dreamstime.com/b/elements-investigation-i-8788315.jpg"
>
In the end, Flurob Burt (if: $sentence is "service")[is now working to atone for his crimes by refilling the tunnels and replacing the floorboards. While Flurob seems content, some may question if this punishment was fitting for the crime comitted. Eventually the tunnels were filled] (if: $sentence is "prison") [is serving his sentence in prison, where he would remain for the next few years. Hopefully this would teach Flurob to never try something like this again, but for now, he must be punished for his crimes](if: $sentence is "death")[was for better or for worse, sentenced to death. Whether or not this was desereved is debatable but it is certain that Flurob will never endanger anyone again,] and all the floor boards were returned and put back in to the floors they were stolen from. Having helped solve the case you have been paid (if: $captureMethod is "tunnelChase" or "chase")[a very nice sum of money for helping apprehend the culprit](else-if: $evidence is "policeSketch" or $captureMethod is "policeReport")[a fair sum of money, though they did admit that you weren't paid as much due to the police doing a lot of the work](else:)[a decent sum of money].

The end


:: Failure {"position":"1600,700","size":"100,100"}
<img
class="fit-picture"
src="https://thumbs.dreamstime.com/b/elements-investigation-i-8788315.jpg"
>
Flurob may have gotten away, but it's not like it matters too much. Floorboards can be replaced, and you still get paid for helping investigate, which is all that matters.

The end


:: Find culprit {"position":"1000,350","size":"100,100"}
<img
class="fit-picture"
src="https://www.shutterstock.com/image-vector/magnifying-glass-icon-white-on-260nw-1059366797.jpg"
>
With the culprit identified, now comes the question of how to catch the culprit.

What method would be best for this situation?

[[Put trackers on the floor boards of several houses]]

[[Find their house and confront them directly]]

(if: $evidence is "tunnelSystem")[[[Show the police the tunnels]]]


:: Find their house and confront them directly {"position":"1200,500","size":"100,100"}
<img
class="fit-picture"
src="https://www.shutterstock.com/image-vector/magnifying-glass-icon-white-on-260nw-1059366797.jpg"
>
After going over the government profile of Flurob Burt, you find his address and go to his house. Knocking on his door, you find that Flurob suprisingly answers the door but refuses to answer any questions. Thankfully, you have a search warrant so you can legally search his home without needing to ask many questions.

(if: $evidence is "tunnelSystem") [Searching the house, you find plans that describe a hidden tunnel system and a map that shows which houses have been stolen from. After taking them, you turn to Flurob to see him running out of his house to try and escape.](if: $evidence is "hairDNA")[In the house, you find another strand of hair which you take while investigating the house. Taking it back to the lab for testing, you find it matches with the other hair you found. When you return to arrest Flurob, you find that he's running away from the house.](if: $evidence is "policeSketch")[Almost immediately, you find that Flurob's face matches almost perfectly with the police sketch. When you tell him that the suspect you're looking for looks almost exactly like him, he immidiately runs out the door to try and tries to escape.]

[[It's not your job to chase down criminals, just tell the police the culprit's running|Tell the police the culprit's running]]

[[But if you chase them down it's unlikely they would escape |Chase them down]]


:: Imprisonment {"position":"2000,350","size":"100,100"}
<img
class="fit-picture"
src="https://tse2.mm.bing.net/th/id/OIP.UyWnzzv2q5T4qkB8LzoxGgHaEK?rs=1&pid=ImgDetMain&o=7&rm=3"
>
(set: $sentence to "prison")
(if: $evidence is "policeSketch" or $captureMethod is "policeReport")[While the jury is unsure why you feel you get a say in Flurob's punishment, as you let the police do most of the work, they agree with your decision. ]No harm may have been intended, but many lives could have been endagered as well as the theft of private property. Due to this, it was unanimously decided that Flurob Burt should face 7 years of imprisonment for his crimes.

[[Ending]]


:: Neighborhood {"position":"800,200","size":"100,100"}
<img
class="fit-picture"
src="https://www.shutterstock.com/image-vector/magnifying-glass-icon-white-on-260nw-1059366797.jpg"
>
(set: $evidence to "hairDNA")
You decide to check the scene of the crime, some of the houses with their floor board stolen.

Going around the neighborhood, you ask the residents if you can investigate the holes in the floors to which most comply. Looking through most holes, the culprit seems clever. Hardly anything that could be seen as solid evidence was left behind.

That being said, there was a single piece of evidence that could be found: a single strand of hair, hidden by the dirt, almost unnoticed by you and clearly unnoticed by the thief. After DNA testing the hair, you find it to match Flurob Burt.

[[Find culprit]]


:: Police station {"position":"800,500","size":"100,100"}
<img
class="fit-picture"
src="https://www.shutterstock.com/image-vector/magnifying-glass-icon-white-on-260nw-1059366797.jpg"
>
(set: $evidence to "policeSketch")
To give yourself as little work as needed, you go to the police station to see what they already have discovered

When asking for information on the case, the police tell you that 2 officers reportedly saw the culprit and was chasing them down as you spoke. Once you knew the location you got there as soon as you could. Once you found the cops chasing the culprit, they admit to losing the culprit in the sewers, but managed to get a good look at their face.

After a sketch artist gets the details, the sketch they made looks like someone who could only be a person named Flurob Burt.

[[Find culprit]]


:: Put the culprit to trial {"position":"1800,350","size":"100,100"}
<img
class="fit-picture"
src="https://tse2.mm.bing.net/th/id/OIP.UyWnzzv2q5T4qkB8LzoxGgHaEK?rs=1&pid=ImgDetMain&o=7&rm=3"
>
Now that you have caught Flurob Burt, he can be put on trial for his crimes. 

(if: $captureMethod is "trackFloors")[Having caught Flurob in the act, the judge and jury both agree that Flurob is guilty beyond reasonable doubt and will serve what ever sentence is given.] (if: $captureMethod is "tunnelChase")[With the discovery of the tunnels the jury and judge decide that Flurob is undeniably guilty, potentially endangering countless civilians if the tunnels were to collapse.] (if: $captureMethod is "policeReport" or "chase")[Although the jury is on the fence on whether the visit to Flurobs house was justified, his reaction is still enough to confirm that he is guilty.]

The only question that remains is what should be his punishment?

[[Community Service]]

[[Imprisonment]]

(if: $evidence is not "policeSketch" and $captureMethod is not "policeReport")[[[Death sentence]]]



:: Put trackers on the floor boards of several houses {"position":"1200,200","size":"100,100"}
<img
class="fit-picture"
src="https://www.shutterstock.com/image-vector/magnifying-glass-icon-white-on-260nw-1059366797.jpg"
>
(set: $captureMethod to "trackFloors")
If Flurob Burt wants the floors so badly, then why not prepare some floors just for him and let him take them?

(if: $evidence is "policeSketch")
[During the day you told officers to plant a device in several houses that would alert the police to the floorboards location. That night, you recieve the report that Flurob has been arrested, and it is confirmed that the police sketch matches Flurob's face.]
(else:)[During the day you and several officers planted a device in several houses that would alert you and the police to the floor boards location. Later that night you get notified of a floorboard starting to move and head to the location immediately. You arrive as the police does, catching and arresting Flurob as he exits an alleyway.]

[[Now that he has been caught, it is time to put the culprit to trial|Put the culprit to trial]]


:: Show the police the tunnels {"position":"1200,350","size":"100,100"}
<img
class="fit-picture"
src="https://www.shutterstock.com/image-vector/magnifying-glass-icon-white-on-260nw-1059366797.jpg"
>
(set: $captureMethod to "tunnelChase")
Thanks to you finding the tunnels, you have an area to concentrate the police into.
That night, before Flurob was able to steal more floors, you and several officers went into the tunnels you found and flooded the area so there was nowhere Flurob could hide.

After a few hours of searching an officer reported that they had seen Flurob and in a matter of minutes, caught Flurob.

[[Now that he has been caught, it is time to put the culprit to trial|Put the culprit to trial]]


:: Story start {"position":"600,350","size":"100,100"}
<img
class="fit-picture"
src="https://www.shutterstock.com/image-vector/magnifying-glass-icon-white-on-260nw-1059366797.jpg"
>
$100000000000000000000000000000000000 worth of floorboards have been stolen. Reportedly, throughout the week people have reported that at various points in the day many houses have had parts of their floors pulled down and stolen. A few people who were in the room when the floors were stolen had checked under the floor and saw a figure running away with the floorboards, but with no dicernable features.

You, a detective, have been hired to find the stolen floors and the culprit who have been stealing them from under everyones noses.

Where do you search first?

[[The Neighborhood would let you survey the houses with stolen floors|Neighborhood]]

[[Alleyways typically are flush with crimes|Alleyway]]

[[A visit to the Police station could get you evidence the police already found|Police station]]


:: Tell the police the culprit's running {"position":"1400,700","size":"100,100"}
<img
class="fit-picture"
src="https://www.shutterstock.com/image-vector/magnifying-glass-icon-white-on-260nw-1059366797.jpg"
>
(if: $evidence is "policeSketch")[Seeing Flurob escape you report to the police that he's running away and the direction he ran to. After that you return take a walk around the neighborhood as you wait for the police to report back to you.

[[When they do, they tell you that Flurob got away|Failure]]]
(else:)[Seeing Flurob escape you report to the police that he's running away and the direction he ran to. As the police track down Flurob, you continue to investigate Flurob's house to see if any other evidence could be found. While you do not find anything, the police report that they have managed to catch and arrest Flurob.
(set: $captureMethod to "policeReport")
[[Now that he has been caught, it is time to put the culprit to trial|Put the culprit to trial]]]


:: \[Death sentence {"position":"1800,600","size":"100,100"}

